# Routing

## Framework semantics

CakePHP maps URLs to controller actions via `config/routes.php` (and plugin route files) using the Router. Dashed/inflected defaults, scopes, prefixes, and resource routes are first-class — not Laravel `Route::` facades or Artisan route lists.

## Required behavior

- Define URL → controller/action mappings in route config; keep controllers free of ad-hoc URL dispatch logic.
- Prefer scoped/prefixed routes and named routes consistent with the app’s existing style.
- Keep route callables thin — no persistence, validation, or authorization decisions inside route closures.
- Use `bin/cake routes` (not Artisan) when inspecting the route table.

## Anti-patterns

- Inventing Eloquent/Laravel router APIs
- Domain/persistence logic inside route definitions
- Duplicating the same path map in controllers

## Review checklist

- [ ] New endpoints have an explicit route or intentional fallback
- [ ] Route files remain declarative (connect/scope/resources only)
- [ ] No Laravel Route facade / artisan mental model
